wasm jit: one continuation block per finally on a multi-finally leave (gex)

A leave that exits several try-finally blocks emitted CALL_HANDLER; CALL_HANDLER; BR
in one block. The wasm emitter runs a finally as "finally_ind = the next OP_BR target,
goto handler", so the first handler had nowhere to return and the method was refused
("finally: complex call_handler continuation"). Under COMPILE_WASM each CALL_HANDLER
but the last now ends its block with a BR to a fresh block, the shape the non-wasm
path already makes for its abort check. Test: T.NestedFinally.

diff --git a/src/mono/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c b/src/mono/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c
index 9dce4a013..2812f8d55 100644
--- a/src/mono/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c
+++ b/src/mono/mono/mini/method-to-ir.c
@@ -12500,6 +12500,29 @@ field_access_end:
 						MONO_START_BB (cfg, dont_throw);
 						cfg->cbb->clause_holes = tmp;
 					}
+					/* COMPILE_WASM, a leave that exits more than one try-finally (gex): give each
+					 * OP_CALL_HANDLER but the last its own continuation block. The wasm emitter
+					 * expresses a handler call as "finally_ind = the following OP_BR's target, goto the
+					 * finally", so CALL_HANDLER; CALL_HANDLER; BR had no place for the first finally to
+					 * come back to and refused the method. The split is the same shape the non-wasm
+					 * path above makes with its dont_throw block, and the new block takes the leave's
+					 * real_offset, so it lands in the same EH region. */
+					if (COMPILE_WASM (cfg)) {
+						GList *rest;
+						for (rest = tmp->next; rest; rest = rest->next)
+							if (((MonoLeaveClause *) rest->data)->clause->flags == MONO_EXCEPTION_CLAUSE_FINALLY)
+								break;
+						if (rest) {
+							MonoBasicBlock *cont;
+							NEW_BBLOCK (cfg, cont);
+							MONO_INST_NEW (cfg, ins, OP_BR);
+							ins->inst_target_bb = cont;
+							MONO_ADD_INS (cfg->cbb, ins);
+							link_bblock (cfg, cfg->cbb, cont);
+							MONO_START_BB (cfg, cont);
+							cfg->cbb->clause_holes = tmp;
+						}
+					}
 					/* COMPILE_WASM: skip the async-abort propagation check — thread abort does not
 					 * exist on wasm (no async suspension of managed code; Thread.Abort is PNSE), and
 					 * the check breaks the leave into a shape the wasm emitter's OP_CALL_HANDLER
